The code confirms the five causes: reference provenance is recorded without an assembly check; restarts lack a directory-wide run fence; region filtering removes paralog evidence; each shard rebuilds universe metadata; and `.done` JSON is accessed before its type is checked.

The existing sentinel has 6,145 rows across 22 shards. I’ll profile bounded synthetic runs and add memory reporting to the sentinel script. The cause of the reported 4.19 GB peak is still unverified.

